/*
DevLens - Database Design (MVP / Target Model)

Related Documents
- 01-business-logic-architecture.md
- 03-backend-roadmap.md
- 04-metric-definitions.md
- 06-api-design.md
- openapi.yaml

Legend
[PG] = PostgreSQL
[CH] = ClickHouse (Logical model only)

Design Goals
- PostgreSQL stores transactional/application state.
- ClickHouse stores event/analytics data and aggregates.
- GitHub App is the primary integration model.
- Dashboard reads calculated data from storage, not GitHub directly.
- Webhook and worker processing must be idempotent.
- The model must support initial sync, resume sync, backfill, metric rebuild,
  data retention, and future provider expansion.
*/

/* ==================================================
1. Design Conventions
================================================== */

/*
Audit Convention

Business / Configuration Tables
- created_at
- created_by
- updated_at
- updated_by
- deleted_at
- deleted_by

Operational Tables
- created_at
- updated_at
- status timestamps that describe execution lifecycle

Analytics Tables
- event_at / metric_date
- ingested_at
- calculated_at
- metric_version where applicable

Notes
- *_by logically refers to users.id.
- Audit references are intentionally not drawn as DBML refs to keep the
  diagram readable.
- Audit user IDs can be null when an action is performed by the system.
*/

/*
Soft Delete Strategy

Soft Delete
- users
- organizations
- github_installations
- repositories
- metric_definitions

Lifecycle / Status instead of Soft Delete
- github_installation_repositories
- sync_jobs
- sync_checkpoints
- webhook_deliveries
- insight_statuses

No Soft Delete
- ClickHouse event tables
- ClickHouse aggregate tables

Reason
- Configuration data may need restore/history.
- Operational and event data should preserve execution/history state.
- Analytics retention should be managed by retention policy / TTL rather
  than CRUD-style soft delete.
*/

/*
Relation Strategy

PostgreSQL
- Use real foreign keys for core business relations.

ClickHouse
- Use logical relationships only.
- Do not draw cross-database foreign-key lines.

Audit Fields
- created_by / updated_by / deleted_by logically reference users.id.
- They intentionally do not use [ref] in this DBML.
*/

/*
Naming Convention

Primary Key
- id

External Provider Identifier
- github_*_id for GitHub-specific source IDs in the current MVP

Foreign Key
- xxx_id

Timestamp
- *_at

Boolean
- is_*

Status
- status
- *_status

Versioned Metrics
- metric_version
- algorithm_version
*/

/* ==================================================
2. PostgreSQL - Identity and Core Domain
================================================== */

Table users {
  id uuid [pk]
  email varchar [not null, unique]
  name varchar
  avatar_url varchar

  status varchar [not null, default: 'active']
  deactivated_at timestamp

  created_at timestamp [not null]
  updated_at timestamp
  deleted_at timestamp
  deleted_by uuid
}

Table organizations {
  id uuid [pk]

  github_id bigint [unique]
  slug varchar [not null, unique]
  name varchar [not null]

  created_at timestamp [not null]
  created_by uuid
  updated_at timestamp
  updated_by uuid
  deleted_at timestamp
  deleted_by uuid
}

Table organization_members {
  id uuid [pk]

  organization_id uuid [not null, ref: > organizations.id]
  user_id uuid [not null, ref: > users.id]

  role varchar [not null]

  created_at timestamp [not null]
  created_by uuid
  updated_at timestamp
  updated_by uuid

  indexes {
    (organization_id, user_id) [unique]
  }
}

/* ==================================================
3. PostgreSQL - GitHub App Integration
================================================== */

/*
GitHub App installation for an organization/account.

Installation access tokens are intentionally NOT stored permanently.
The backend generates/caches short-lived installation tokens at runtime.
*/
Table github_installations {
  id uuid [pk]

  organization_id uuid [not null, ref: > organizations.id]
  installation_id bigint [not null, unique]

  account_login varchar [not null]
  account_type varchar
  target_type varchar

  status varchar [not null]
  permissions_json json

  installed_by_github_user_id bigint
  installed_at timestamp [not null]
  suspended_at timestamp
  disconnected_at timestamp

  created_at timestamp [not null]
  created_by uuid
  updated_at timestamp
  updated_by uuid
  deleted_at timestamp
  deleted_by uuid
}

/*
Snapshot/state of repositories accessible through one GitHub installation.

This table is the source for the frontend "accessible repositories" flow
before a repository is selected for DevLens monitoring.
*/
Table github_installation_repositories {
  id uuid [pk]

  github_installation_id uuid [not null, ref: > github_installations.id]
  github_repository_id bigint [not null]

  full_name varchar [not null]
  private boolean [not null]
  default_branch varchar

  installation_status varchar [not null]
  selection_status varchar [not null]

  permissions_json json

  last_discovered_at timestamp
  last_synced_at timestamp
  sync_error_message text

  created_at timestamp [not null]
  updated_at timestamp

  indexes {
    (github_installation_id, github_repository_id) [unique]
  }
}

/*
Repository selected by the user and actively managed by DevLens.
*/
Table repositories {
  id uuid [pk]

  organization_id uuid [not null, ref: > organizations.id]
  github_installation_repository_id uuid [ref: > github_installation_repositories.id]

  github_id bigint [not null, unique]
  name varchar [not null]
  full_name varchar [not null, unique]
  default_branch varchar

  is_active boolean [not null, default: true]
  archived_at timestamp

  last_synced_at timestamp
  initial_sync_status varchar
  initial_sync_completed_at timestamp
  sync_error_message text

  created_at timestamp [not null]
  created_by uuid
  updated_at timestamp
  updated_by uuid
  deleted_at timestamp
  deleted_by uuid
}

/* ==================================================
4. PostgreSQL - Sync and Webhook Operations
================================================== */

Table sync_jobs {
  id uuid [pk]

  repository_id uuid [not null, ref: > repositories.id]

  job_type varchar [not null]
  status varchar [not null]
  progress int [not null, default: 0]

  idempotency_key varchar
  triggered_by uuid

  error_code varchar
  error_message text

  started_at timestamp
  finished_at timestamp

  created_at timestamp [not null]
  updated_at timestamp

  indexes {
    idempotency_key
    (repository_id, status)
  }
}

/*
Checkpoint allows initial/incremental sync to resume without restarting the
entire repository sync.

Examples:
- pull_requests page/cursor
- reviews page/cursor
- changed_files page/cursor
- workflows page/cursor
- deployments page/cursor
*/
Table sync_checkpoints {
  id uuid [pk]

  sync_job_id uuid [not null, ref: > sync_jobs.id]
  repository_id uuid [not null, ref: > repositories.id]

  resource_type varchar [not null]
  checkpoint_key varchar [not null]
  checkpoint_value text

  status varchar [not null]
  last_processed_at timestamp

  created_at timestamp [not null]
  updated_at timestamp

  indexes {
    (sync_job_id, resource_type, checkpoint_key) [unique]
    (repository_id, resource_type)
  }
}

/*
GitHub webhook delivery log.

github_delivery_id provides hard idempotency for GitHub retries.
Webhook handlers should validate/store/enqueue quickly and avoid heavy
processing in the HTTP request.
*/
Table webhook_deliveries {
  id uuid [pk]

  repository_id uuid [ref: > repositories.id]
  github_installation_id uuid [ref: > github_installations.id]
  sync_job_id uuid [ref: > sync_jobs.id]

  github_delivery_id varchar [not null, unique]
  event_type varchar [not null]
  action varchar

  processing_status varchar [not null]
  retry_count int [not null, default: 0]
  next_retry_at timestamp
  payload json
  payload_retention_until timestamp

  error_message text

  received_at timestamp [not null]
  processed_at timestamp

  created_at timestamp [not null]
  updated_at timestamp
}

/* ==================================================
5. PostgreSQL - Governance and Metric Configuration
================================================== */

Table audit_logs {
  id uuid [pk]

  organization_id uuid [ref: > organizations.id]
  actor_user_id uuid

  action varchar [not null]
  resource_type varchar [not null]
  resource_id uuid

  metadata_json json

  created_at timestamp [not null]

  indexes {
    (organization_id, created_at)
    (resource_type, resource_id)
  }
}

/*
Versioned metric definition/configuration.

Formula text is descriptive metadata. Runtime calculation logic remains in
versioned application code, while this table records which definition/version
is active and supports rebuild/auditability.
*/
Table metric_definitions {
  id uuid [pk]

  metric_key varchar [not null]
  name varchar [not null]

  metric_version int [not null]
  algorithm_version varchar

  unit varchar
  description text
  config_json json

  is_active boolean [not null, default: true]

  created_at timestamp [not null]
  created_by uuid
  updated_at timestamp
  updated_by uuid
  deleted_at timestamp
  deleted_by uuid

  indexes {
    (metric_key, metric_version) [unique]
  }
}

/*
State for generated insights.

Insights themselves may be rebuilt from analytics data; this table stores
application-level state such as reviewed/dismissed/reopened.
*/
Table insight_statuses {
  id uuid [pk]

  organization_id uuid [not null, ref: > organizations.id]
  repository_id uuid [ref: > repositories.id]

  insight_key varchar [not null]
  insight_type varchar [not null]
  status varchar [not null]

  evidence_json json

  reviewed_by uuid
  reviewed_at timestamp
  dismissed_at timestamp
  reopened_at timestamp

  created_at timestamp [not null]
  updated_at timestamp

  indexes {
    (organization_id, insight_key) [unique]
    (repository_id, status)
  }
}

/* ==================================================
6. ClickHouse - Event Data
================================================== */

/*
ClickHouse Notes

- These tables are logical analytics models.
- No PostgreSQL-style foreign keys.
- repository_id and other UUIDs logically reference PostgreSQL/core entities.
- Event tables must tolerate duplicate and late-arriving GitHub events.
- Physical ENGINE / PARTITION BY / ORDER BY / TTL are implementation concerns
  and should be finalized in ClickHouse migration/schema files.
*/

/*
Normalized Pull Request event/state observations.
Logical Relation: repository_id -> repositories.id
*/
Table pull_request_events {
  event_id uuid
  repository_id uuid

  github_pr_id bigint
  pull_request_number int

  author_login varchar
  state varchar
  is_draft boolean

  event_type varchar
  event_action varchar

  pr_created_at timestamp
  merged_at timestamp
  closed_at timestamp

  additions int
  deletions int
  files_changed int

  source_delivery_id varchar
  event_at timestamp
  ingested_at timestamp
}

/*
Normalized review event/state observations.
Logical Relation: repository_id -> repositories.id
Logical Relation: github_pr_id -> pull_request_events.github_pr_id
*/
Table review_events {
  event_id uuid
  repository_id uuid

  github_pr_id bigint
  github_review_id bigint

  reviewer_login varchar
  reviewer_type varchar
  state varchar

  review_requested_at timestamp
  review_submitted_at timestamp

  source_delivery_id varchar
  event_at timestamp
  ingested_at timestamp
}

/*
Commit-level events required for churn, workload context, rebuilds and future
metrics. DevLens should not store source code content.
*/
Table commit_events {
  event_id uuid
  repository_id uuid

  github_commit_sha varchar

  author_login varchar
  author_type varchar

  additions int
  deletions int
  files_changed int

  committed_at timestamp
  event_at timestamp
  ingested_at timestamp
}

/*
GitHub Actions / workflow execution observations.
*/
Table workflow_events {
  event_id uuid
  repository_id uuid

  github_workflow_run_id bigint
  workflow_name varchar

  status varchar
  conclusion varchar

  started_at timestamp
  completed_at timestamp

  source_delivery_id varchar
  event_at timestamp
  ingested_at timestamp
}

/*
Deployment / deployment-status observations.
*/
Table deployment_events {
  event_id uuid
  repository_id uuid

  github_deployment_id bigint
  environment varchar
  status varchar

  deployed_at timestamp

  source_delivery_id varchar
  event_at timestamp
  ingested_at timestamp
}

/*
Changed-file observations used by PR Size, Code Churn and Hotspot Score.
*/
Table file_change_events {
  event_id uuid
  repository_id uuid

  github_pr_id bigint
  github_commit_sha varchar

  file_path varchar
  change_type varchar

  additions int
  deletions int
  commit_count int

  event_at timestamp
  ingested_at timestamp
}

/* ==================================================
7. ClickHouse - Aggregate / Metric Data
================================================== */

/*
Primary repository/day aggregate used by dashboard range queries.

Count fields are stored to avoid incorrect "average of daily averages".
*/
Table repository_daily_metrics {
  repository_id uuid
  metric_date date

  metric_version int

  pr_cycle_time_minutes decimal
  review_wait_minutes decimal
  average_review_minutes decimal

  average_files_changed decimal
  average_additions decimal
  average_deletions decimal

  deployment_frequency decimal
  change_failure_rate decimal
  review_coverage decimal

  pr_count int
  merged_pr_count int
  reviewed_pr_count int

  review_wait_sample_count int
  review_time_sample_count int

  successful_deployment_count int
  failed_deployment_count int

  calculated_at timestamp
}

/*
Per-PR calculated metric projection for drilldown and rebuild validation.
*/
Table pull_request_metrics {
  repository_id uuid
  github_pr_id bigint
  pull_request_number int

  metric_version int

  cycle_time_minutes decimal
  review_wait_minutes decimal
  review_time_minutes decimal

  files_changed int
  additions int
  deletions int

  calculated_at timestamp
}

/*
Daily reviewer distribution / process metrics.

Used for workload distribution and review concentration analysis.
This table is not a developer ranking table.
*/
Table reviewer_daily_metrics {
  repository_id uuid
  metric_date date

  reviewer_login varchar
  reviewer_type varchar

  review_count int
  reviewed_pr_count int
  average_review_minutes decimal

  metric_version int
  calculated_at timestamp
}

/*
File-level hotspot projection by repository/date.
*/
Table hotspot_metrics {
  repository_id uuid
  metric_date date

  file_path varchar

  change_count int
  code_churn int
  commit_count int
  hotspot_score decimal

  metric_version int
  calculated_at timestamp
}

/* ==================================================
8. Main Logical Relations
==================================================

PostgreSQL

users
- organization_members.user_id

organizations
- organization_members.organization_id
- github_installations.organization_id
- repositories.organization_id
- audit_logs.organization_id
- insight_statuses.organization_id

github_installations
- github_installation_repositories.github_installation_id
- webhook_deliveries.github_installation_id

github_installation_repositories
- repositories.github_installation_repository_id

repositories
- sync_jobs.repository_id
- sync_checkpoints.repository_id
- webhook_deliveries.repository_id
- insight_statuses.repository_id

sync_jobs
- sync_checkpoints.sync_job_id
- webhook_deliveries.sync_job_id


ClickHouse Logical Relations

repositories
- pull_request_events.repository_id
- review_events.repository_id
- commit_events.repository_id
- workflow_events.repository_id
- deployment_events.repository_id
- file_change_events.repository_id
- repository_daily_metrics.repository_id
- pull_request_metrics.repository_id
- reviewer_daily_metrics.repository_id
- hotspot_metrics.repository_id
*/

/* ==================================================
9. Metric Mapping
==================================================

PR Cycle Time
- pull_request_events.pr_created_at
- pull_request_events.merged_at
- pull_request_metrics.cycle_time_minutes
- repository_daily_metrics.pr_cycle_time_minutes
- repository_daily_metrics.merged_pr_count

Review Wait Time
- review_events.review_requested_at
- review_events.review_submitted_at / first valid review event
- pull_request_metrics.review_wait_minutes
- repository_daily_metrics.review_wait_minutes
- repository_daily_metrics.review_wait_sample_count

Review Time
- review_events.review_requested_at
- review_events.review_submitted_at
- pull_request_metrics.review_time_minutes
- repository_daily_metrics.average_review_minutes
- repository_daily_metrics.review_time_sample_count

PR Size
- pull_request_events.files_changed
- pull_request_events.additions
- pull_request_events.deletions
- pull_request_metrics.files_changed
- pull_request_metrics.additions
- pull_request_metrics.deletions
- repository_daily_metrics.average_files_changed
- repository_daily_metrics.average_additions
- repository_daily_metrics.average_deletions

Deployment Frequency
- deployment_events.status
- deployment_events.deployed_at
- repository_daily_metrics.successful_deployment_count
- repository_daily_metrics.deployment_frequency

Change Failure Rate
- deployment_events.status
- repository_daily_metrics.successful_deployment_count
- repository_daily_metrics.failed_deployment_count
- repository_daily_metrics.change_failure_rate

Review Coverage
- pull_request_events.github_pr_id
- review_events.github_pr_id
- repository_daily_metrics.pr_count
- repository_daily_metrics.reviewed_pr_count
- repository_daily_metrics.review_coverage

Hotspot Score
- file_change_events.file_path
- file_change_events.additions
- file_change_events.deletions
- file_change_events.commit_count
- hotspot_metrics.change_count
- hotspot_metrics.code_churn
- hotspot_metrics.commit_count
- hotspot_metrics.hotspot_score

Workload Distribution (Planned)
- pull_request_events.author_login
- review_events.reviewer_login
- reviewer_daily_metrics.review_count
- reviewer_daily_metrics.reviewed_pr_count
*/

/* ==================================================
10. Data Flow
==================================================

GitHub App
  |
  +--> Installation / Accessible Repositories
  |        |
  |        v
  |   PostgreSQL
  |   - github_installations
  |   - github_installation_repositories
  |   - repositories
  |
  +--> Initial Sync / Webhook
           |
           v
      NATS JetStream
           |
           v
        Workers
           |
      +----+----------------------+
      |                           |
      v                           v
 PostgreSQL                  ClickHouse
 - sync_jobs                 - *_events
 - checkpoints               - raw normalized analytics
 - webhook log
                                  |
                                  v
                             Metric Worker
                                  |
                     +------------+-------------+
                     |            |             |
                     v            v             v
             repository_daily  PR metrics   hotspot/reviewer
                 metrics
                     |
                     v
                Go Dashboard API
                     |
                     v
               React Frontend
*/

/* ==================================================
11. Implementation Notes
==================================================

- This file describes the target logical model based on the latest business
  architecture and backend roadmap.
- Current implementation may still contain transitional PostgreSQL tables for
  pull_requests, pull_request_reviews, deployments or file_changes.
- Do not silently rewrite existing production migrations to match this target
  model. Use explicit migrations and data-migration/backfill plans.
- ClickHouse physical schema (ENGINE, PARTITION BY, ORDER BY, TTL) must be
  defined in ClickHouse migration/schema files, not inferred only from DBML.
- GitHub installation access tokens must remain short-lived and must not be
  persisted as long-lived secrets in these tables.
- Future GitLab/Bitbucket support should introduce provider-agnostic canonical
  event models without breaking existing metric contracts.
*/
